Z||000006||fropuff||09-22-2001||01:39 PM||||Well, that right there is what happens when you get hit by a Dodge 3500 15-passenger van buzzing through the parking lot.  I was backing out of my spot, and I checked my blind spots MANY TIMES.  I did NOT see anyone coming; I must have looked four times each way.  I do every time.  Anyway, I was checking the left front so I didn't clip the curb, and I saw something behind me.  I slammed on the brakes, and I was STOPPED, when I heard a crash.  So I LEFT THE CAR WHERE IT WAS, and got out.  So did the other guy.  First thing he said was: "Where did you come from?"  He didn't see me I guess.  A little while later, he said: "Well, I'm kinda in a hurry."  How about that.  So I had to let him go.  But I did get his name and phone number.  I know; I should have made him stay.  He had on a temp. plate, so me and another guy went to the dealer his wife bought the van from.  They gave me her name and a DIFFERENT number.  So the cops got to the lot, and I told them my story.  A few days later, we got a call from the cop; the police report was done.  He got his story, but also said that the guy got a citation for not having a MN driver's license and an IL revoked license.  Then we got the police report.  On it, he said that I tried to SQUEEZE by him, nevermind that his damage was in front of the wheel on the same side as my damage.  He also said that I told him that it was my fault.  Huh.  Long story short  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> we go to court on the 18th of October.  Damages were $2783.10, but I think I will fix it either way it goes.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000007||KissMySSFiero||09-22-2001||02:16 PM||||sorry too hear that man....i know its too late now but whenever you get in a wreck wait for a witness or a cop to get to the scene.  if he doesnt want to wait then i think he would get in trouble for fleeing the scene of an accident.  now its just your word against his.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||09-22-2001||09:31 PM||||I know; I should have had him stay.  But, it wasn't like I could keep him there against his will.  He just didn't want to stay at all.  I think that I'll be able to prove him wrong.  #1 is that he had no license.  Kinda hard to get into an accident when you're not supposed to drive.  He also gave me a fake name and number.  I have the paper that he gave me, and his actual name and number on the police report.  I'm going to get a copy of the citation for not having a license as well.  I think I'll be able to prove that I couldn't have tried to squeeze by him, like he said.  I would have to be backing up for both of us to have the damage where it is.  I also have a witness that saw where the cars were parked.  No one saw the actual accident, but the gas station manager came out and saw where the cars were.  I might have him sign something.  I'm also getting a diagram of the lot to show where we were.  I can't proce many things, but I can prove the guy wrong.  What else should I get?  Thanks.    ||||reg||1
